Privacy Policy
Last Updated: 29 July 2026

Daily Grace: Bible Affirmations ("the App") is operated by Anoushka Studios. This Privacy Policy explains how we handle your data. Our principle is simple: we collect the minimum necessary, and nothing that personally identifies you.

Information We Collect
The App does not require account creation and does not collect personally identifiable information — no name, no email address, no contact details, no precise location. Journal reflections you write are stored only on your device and are never transmitted to our servers. Your streak count, favorites, and settings are stored locally using iOS device storage.

Notifications
If you enable reminder notifications, they are scheduled locally on your device. No notification data is sent to external servers, and no push tokens are collected.

In-App Purchases
Daily Grace offers a one-time purchase to unlock Pro. Payments are processed through Apple's App Store. We do not store or have access to your payment information. Purchase history is managed through your Apple ID. To manage purchases and entitlements, the App uses RevenueCat, a third-party service that receives an anonymous app user ID, device information, and your purchase history (never your name, email, or payment details). RevenueCat processes this data on our behalf to validate purchases and restore them across your devices. See RevenueCat's privacy policy at https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy.

Analytics
The App uses PostHog, a third-party analytics service, to understand how the App is used so we can improve it. PostHog receives an anonymous, randomly generated device identifier along with basic usage events such as opening the App, completing onboarding, saving a journal entry, enabling a reminder, and viewing or completing a purchase. These events carry limited context — for example your current streak length, the theme category of an entry, and whether you have purchased Pro. We never send the text of your journal reflections, your name, your email, or your payment details. Your IP address is used by PostHog to derive an approximate country and is not stored by us. We do not use advertising SDKs, and we do not track you across other apps or websites. See PostHog's privacy policy at https://posthog.com/privacy.

Diagnostics and Error Reports
If the App encounters an unexpected error, a diagnostic report is sent to PostHog so we can find and fix the problem. These reports contain only technical information about the failure itself — the error type, the error message, and the technical stack trace identifying the code involved — together with the same anonymous device identifier used for analytics. They never include the text of your journal reflections, your name, your email, or your payment details.

Home Screen Widget
If you add the Daily Grace widget to your Home Screen, the App shares today's affirmation and your Pro status with the widget through Apple's App Group storage. This data never leaves your device.

Data Sharing
Other than the purchase processing and analytics described above, we do not sell, trade, or transfer your data to third parties.

Data Security
All content you create in the App, including your journal reflections, is stored on your device and protected by iOS security mechanisms including device encryption. The limited analytics events described above are transmitted over an encrypted connection.

Children's Privacy
The App is rated 13+ on the App Store. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under the age of 13.

Changes to This Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any updates will be reflected by revising the "Last Updated" date above.

